{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 85, :comments ["<b>One hundred thirty, the one bowl, etc.</b> Why is this said? Because 'one hundred thirty' is stated without specifying in which shekel, therefore he repeated and specified it here, and included it in all of them — <b>all the silver of the vessels, by the shekel of the sanctuary</b>." "<b>All the silver of the vessels, etc.</b> It teaches you that the sanctuary vessels were precisely weighted — weighing them one by one, and weighing them all together — neither more nor less (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:53.306992846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}